{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-15T08:56:05.083Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"dd8c1bbe6971b2611016f79f","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-15T08:56:05.083Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"Cause: pm-ops 2026.10.14 readSubstitution resets single/double quote state at every newline. The multiline single-quoted jq filter contains parentheses spanning lines; later GraphQL mutation text is misclassified as unresolved executable expansion. This is a false positive: gh api graphql only queries/resolves review threads. Fix: replace exactly that workflow block with a plain node scripts/resolve-release-threads.ts invocation; helper retains the original GraphQL documents, jq policy, serial mutations, best-effort failures and summary text. Surrounding release workflow is unchanged. Focused helper tests pass 5/5 and the canonical verifier passes without changes or exemptions."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-15T08:56:05.083Z"}],"before_hash":"d189e84fe8fb1981d303845408e33b190c061261d3238383e7de96c872d6b9b1","after_hash":"005eea93c5c8d1fa716be271d8ff4fbb28cb942a1a3267ce0da8e9d58cd7a7f7","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"c2e497d996e961ac1138e5ab0d7aebd57aee1fc29da8b0fa0149c5be526a931c"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-15T08:57:43.166Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"dd8c1bbe6971b2611016f79f","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-15T08:57:43.166Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"Revert proof: restoring only the original workflow makes the tracked-repository attestation test fail 0/1; replacing only resolveReleaseThreads with a no-op makes the query/mutation regression fail 0/1. Both restored fixes pass. Byte comparison confirms that every workflow byte outside the extracted block is unchanged. Smaller reproduction confirms parentheses spanning lines are not required: multiline single-quoted --jq text inside a quoted command substitution followed by a redirected GraphQL mutation is sufficient; readSubstitution loses quote state at the newline."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-15T08:57:43.166Z"}],"before_hash":"005eea93c5c8d1fa716be271d8ff4fbb28cb942a1a3267ce0da8e9d58cd7a7f7","after_hash":"5aeeb3e3b411d412a26a024eb8d6c509a53702b8dade65844a177a3457bd8830","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"13e146638d2c8c340c5c7973bc99f1745959126d26a24aa60be391b852440e4b"}
